WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.182
Iterator validity and thread safety are related concerns, but they are not the same concern.

2
00:00:05.182 --> 00:00:12.782
A container can provide valid iterators in single-threaded code and still be unsafe when another thread mutates the container during traversal.

3
00:00:12.782 --> 00:00:20.382
The iterator may have been valid at the start of the loop and become invalid because concurrent code changed the underlying range.

4
00:00:20.382 --> 00:00:23.145
Shared ownership does not automatically solve this problem.

5
00:00:23.145 --> 00:00:32.127
A shared pointer to a container can keep the container object alive, but it does not by itself synchronize access to the container's elements or

6
00:00:32.127 --> 00:00:32.818
internal structure.

7
00:00:32.818 --> 00:00:38.691
Safe concurrent traversal requires an explicit synchronization strategy, immutable snapshots, message passing, or another design that controls

8
00:00:38.691 --> 00:00:39.036
mutation.

9
00:00:39.036 --> 00:00:41.800
Async callbacks and worker tasks deserve special attention.

10
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:48.018
They may capture iterators, references, views, or spans and use them after the owning component has moved on.

11
00:00:48.018 --> 00:00:54.927
Shutdown and cancellation paths are especially risky because containers may be cleared while deferred work is still queued or running.

12
00:00:54.927 --> 00:00:58.382
Defensive code documents the concurrency rule near the data structure.

13
00:00:58.382 --> 00:01:07.018
It should be clear who may read, who may mutate, what lock or ownership rule applies, and whether iterators can be retained across callbacks or

14
00:01:07.018 --> 00:01:07.709
thread boundaries.

15
00:01:07.709 --> 00:01:11.509
Hidden concurrency assumptions are hard to test and harder to debug.

16
00:01:11.509 --> 00:01:14.618
When in doubt, prefer designs that shorten iterator lifetime.

17
00:01:14.618 --> 00:01:22.564
Complete traversal while the synchronization rule is active, copy the data needed by the worker, or pass stable identifiers that can be validated

18
00:01:22.564 --> 00:01:23.600
when work executes.
